--!strict
--!optimize 2
--!lint ConstLocal

const .{
    elements.{ Heading, Paragraph, UnorderedList, ListItem, Link, Strong, Table },
    components.{ Code, CodeBlock, SourceSpan, Squiggle },
    site.{ Page, TableOfContents },
} = require("@chimera")
const .{ h1, h2 } = Heading

const UPSTREAM_RFCS = "https://github.com/luwu-community/luwu/blob/master/rfcs/UPSTREAM.md"

--- The parse error Luwu reports for a table comprehension in a `.luau` file, as luwu-analyze prints it.
const COMPREHENSION_ERROR = table.concat({
    "SyntaxError: Table comprehensions are a Luwu-only feature.\n",
    "\n",
    "Help (Luwu-only feature):\n",
    "  • Consider migrating to a .luwu module if this environment supports Luwu\n",
    "  • Alternatively, you may transpile Luwu code to Luau code via the 'ast' library; ",
    "see Luwu documentation on existing transpilers and usage",
})

const extension_header = Table.header()
    :column("Extension")
    :column("Language")
const extension = Table.row_for(extension_header)

return Page("Compatibility", {
    h1("Compatibility"),
    Paragraph({
        "A Luau library written for Luau 0.730 or earlier runs in Luwu without changes. ",
        "The reverse doesn't hold: once a file uses classes or table comprehensions it's Luwu code, and upstream ",
        "Luau can't run it. Luwu keeps the two apart by file extension, and it refuses Luwu syntax in a ",
        Code(".luau", "plaintext"),
        " file so that file stays valid Luau.",
    }),
    TableOfContents(),

    h2("Luau code in Luwu"),
    Paragraph({
        "Luwu accepts valid Luau code up to and including Luau 0.730, and with it every RFC upstream accepted by ",
        "2026-07-17. RFCs accepted upstream after 0.730 aren't covered by that guarantee. ",
        Link("UPSTREAM.md", UPSTREAM_RFCS):new_tab(),
        " in the Luwu repository lists which upstream RFCs Luwu implements, which it replaced and which it skipped.",
    }),

    h2("Where Luau and Luwu diverge"),
    Paragraph({
        "Since the fork, Luau and Luwu have diverged. The main differences today are in classes and ",
        "inheritance, integers, and destructuring:",
    }),
    UnorderedList({
        ListItem({
            Strong("Classes and inheritance."), " Upstream's ",
            Link("classes RFC", "https://github.com/luau-lang/rfcs/pull/242"):new_tab(),
            " adds implementation inheritance through ", Code("open class"), " and ", Code("extends"),
            ". Its private members have to start with ", Code("_"), " and are read through new ", Code("._"),
            " and ", Code(":_"), " operators that only exist inside methods. Luwu's classes have no inheritance ",
            "and share code through traits instead. Private members keep ordinary names, and every method call ",
            "checks that ", Code("self"), " really is an object of its class.",
        }),
        ListItem({
            Strong("Integers."), " Upstream's ",
            Link(
                "64-bit integer type",
                "https://github.com/luau-lang/rfcs/blob/master/docs/type-long-integer.md"
            ):new_tab(),
            " is a single signed ", Code("integer"), " with no arithmetic operators: adding two of them takes ",
            Code("integer.add(a, b)"), ". It was never enabled on Roblox and isn't covered by Luau's compatibility ",
            "promise. Luwu is building its own, with separate signed and unsigned types, arithmetic operators ",
            "and bigints.",
        }),
        ListItem({
            Strong("Destructuring."), " Upstream accepted key destructuring in 2024 and withdrew it a month later. ",
            "Its ", Link("current proposal", "https://github.com/luau-lang/rfcs/pull/260"):new_tab(),
            " mirrors table constructors, so every name is written twice: ",
            Code("local {name = name, kind = kind} = entry", "luau"), ". In Luwu you write each name once with ",
            Code("const .{ name, kind } = entry"), ", and it works on tables, objects and userdata alike.",
        }),
    }),

    h2("File extensions"),
    Paragraph({
        "Every module has a language, and Luwu takes it from the file's extension. The command-line tools and the ",
        "language server agree on it:",
    }),
    Table(extension_header):rows({
        extension(Code(".luwu", "plaintext"), "Luwu"),
        extension(Code(".luau", "plaintext"), "Luau"),
        extension(Code(".lua", "plaintext"), "Lua"),
    }),
    Paragraph({
        "A project can mix them freely. A ", Code(".luwu", "plaintext"), " module can require a ",
        Code(".luau", "plaintext"), " one, and the other way around.",
    }),

    h2("Luwu syntax in Luau files"),
    Paragraph({
        "Luwu could accept its own syntax everywhere, but then a ", Code(".luau", "plaintext"),
        " file could quietly stop being Luau. It would still run in Luwu and break the day someone opens it in ",
        "upstream tooling, or in Roblox. So Luwu refuses: in a ", Code(".luau", "plaintext"),
        " module, Luwu-only syntax is a parse error that says what to do instead.",
    }),
    CodeBlock([====[
        local fruit = { "apple", "kiwi", "pear" }

        local long_names = { for _, name in fruit when #name > 4 give name }
        table.drop(fruit, "kiwi")
        print(#long_names, #fruit)
    ]====], "luau")
        :line_numbers()
        :squiggle(
            Squiggle.error(SourceSpan.on_line(3, 22, 24), COMPREHENSION_ERROR),
            Squiggle.warning(
                SourceSpan.on_line(4, 1, 10),
                "LuwuOnlyApi: 'table.drop' only exists in Luwu, but this is a Luau file; rename it to '.luwu' if "
                    .. "it's Luwu code"
            )
        ),
    Paragraph({
        "Both messages come straight from ", Code("luwu-analyze", "bash"), " with the file saved as ",
        Code("inventory.luau", "plaintext"), ". Rename it to ", Code("inventory.luwu", "plaintext"),
        " and the same code checks cleanly.",
    }),
    Paragraph({
        "The parser can't reject library functions because they aren't syntax. Instead the ", Code("LuwuOnlyApi"),
        " lint warns about Luwu-only functions like ", Code("table.drop"), " and ", Code("class.of"),
        " in Luau and Lua files. The language server does the same for Luwu-only directives such as ",
        Code("--!trust"), ".",
    }),

    h2("luwuOnly"),
    Paragraph({
        "Behind those errors, the parser marks every syntax node that only Luwu accepts with a ", Code("luwuOnly"),
        " flag. It goes on the smallest node whose own syntax is Luwu's, so a default argument marks its function ",
        "but leaves the function's body alone. Children of a marked node aren't marked unless their own syntax ",
        "is Luwu-only as well.",
    }),
    Paragraph({
        "Tools can read the flag through Luwu's AST reflection (", Code("node:luwuOnly()"),
        "). That's how a transpiler from Luwu to Luau finds exactly the nodes it has to rewrite and leaves ",
        "everything else as it was.",
    }),
})
